{"name":"Willow Tree Mouse","hex":"#c8d5bb","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"willow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various deciduous trees or shrubs in the genus Salix, in the willow family Salicaceae, found primarily on moist soils in cooler zones in the northern hemisphere.","The wood of these trees."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To open and cleanse (cotton, flax, wool, etc.) by means of a willow.","To form a shape or move in a way similar to the long, slender branches of a willow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/willow"},{"term":"tree","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A perennial woody plant taller and larger than a shrub with a wooden trunk and, at some distance from the ground, having leaves and branches.","Any other plant (such as a large shrub or herb) that is reminiscent of the above in form and size."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To chase (an animal or person) up a tree.","To place in a tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tree"},{"term":"mouse","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any mammal of the many rodent families (especially Muridae) that have a small body and a long tail.","Such a rodent that is of the genus Mus."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move cautiously or furtively, in the manner of a mouse (the rodent) (frequently used in the phrasal verb to mouse around).","To hunt or catch mice (the rodents), usually of cats. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mouse"}],"entries":[{"title":"Willow","blocks":[{"text":"Willows, also called sallows and osiers, of the genus Salix, comprise around 350 species of typically deciduous trees and shrubs. They are primarily found on moist soils in cold and temperate regions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Salix_alba_Morton.jpg/330px-Salix_alba_Morton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willow","wikidata":"Q36050"},{"title":"Tree","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a tree is a perennial plant with an elongated stem, or trunk, usually supporting branches and leaves. In some usages, the definition of a tree may be narrower, e.g., including only woody plants with secondary growth, only plants that are usable for timber, or only plants above a specified height. Wider definitions include taller palms, tree ferns, bananas, and bamboos."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree","wikidata":"Q10884"},{"title":"Mouse","blocks":[{"text":"A mouse is a small rodent, characteristically known to have a pointed snout, small rounded ears, a body-length scaly tail, and a high breeding rate. The best known mouse species is the common house mouse. Mice are widely available as pets, but not as popular as some other rodents. In some places, certain kinds of field mice are locally common. They are known to invade homes for food and shelter."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/%D0%9C%D1%8B%D1%88%D1%8C_2.jpg/330px-%D0%9C%D1%8B%D1%88%D1%8C_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mouse","wikidata":"Q2751034"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Salix_silesiaca_a5.jpg/500px-Salix_silesiaca_a5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Salix_silesiaca_a5.jpg/500px-Salix_silesiaca_a5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"At the base of the petiole, a pair of stipules form. These may fall in spring, or last for much of the summer or even for more than one year (marcescence).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASalix_silesiaca_a5.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Young-catkin.jpg/500px-Young-catkin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Young-catkin.jpg/500px-Young-catkin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Young male catkin","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYoung-catkin.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Bourgoyen_knotted_willow_and_woodpile.jpg/500px-Bourgoyen_knotted_willow_and_woodpile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Bourgoyen_knotted_willow_and_woodpile.jpg/1280px-Bourgoyen_knotted_willow_and_woodpile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Bourgoyen_knotted_willow_and_woodpile.jpg/500px-Bourgoyen_knotted_willow_and_woodpile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pollard willow and woodpile in the Bourgoyen-Ossemeersen, Ghent, Belgium","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABourgoyen_knotted_willow_and_woodpile.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Kopfweiden_1.jpg/500px-Kopfweiden_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Kopfweiden_1.jpg/1280px-Kopfweiden_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Kopfweiden_1.jpg/500px-Kopfweiden_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Berlin Britzer Garten polla